# `git archive` substitutes $Format:...$ placeholders in files marked export-subst.
# The Windows verification script stamps the commit it was exported from and
# prints it, so a stale archive is obvious in the first few lines of output
# instead of being mistaken for a behaviour difference on the Windows host.
scripts/verify-windows.ps1 export-subst

# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would give a clone CRLF
# working-tree copies of templates/*.py. Those are copied verbatim into the
# generated package, so the output would stop being byte-identical across
# platforms (ADR-0001) even though every generator pins newline="\n".
*.py text eol=lf
